Kubernetes API Versions and Categories
1️⃣ Core API Group (Application Basics)
apiVersion: v1

This is the core (legacy) API group.

Used for:

Pod: Smallest deployable unit.

Service: Expose applications internally/externally.

ConfigMap: App configuration.

Secret: Sensitive data.

Namespace: Logical isolation.

Node: Cluster nodes.

PersistentVolumeClaim: Storage request.

Example
apiVersion: v1
kind: Service
metadata:
  name: my-service
spec:
  type: ClusterIP
  selector:
    app: myapp
  ports:
    - port: 80

2️⃣ Workloads / Application Deployment
apiVersion: apps/v1

Used for managing workloads and deploying applications.

Used for:

Deployment: Stateless apps.

StatefulSet: Stateful apps, including databases.

DaemonSet: One pod per node.

ReplicaSet: Pod replication.

Example
apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: Deployment
metadata:
  name: nginx
spec:
  replicas: 3
  selector:
    matchLabels:
      app: nginx
  template:
    metadata:
      labels:
        app: nginx
    spec:
      containers:
        - name: nginx
          image: nginx

3️⃣ Networking APIs
apiVersion: networking.k8s.io/v1

Controls traffic flow inside and outside the cluster.

Used for:

Ingress: HTTP/HTTPS routing.

NetworkPolicy: Pod-to-pod traffic rules.

Example
apiVersion: networking.k8s.io/v1
kind: Ingress
metadata:
  name: app-ingress
spec:
  rules:
    - host: myapp.example.com
      http:
        paths:
          - path: /
            pathType: Prefix
            backend:
              service:
                name: my-service
                port:
                  number: 80

4️⃣ Storage / Database Related APIs
apiVersion: storage.k8s.io/v1

Defines storage classes, volumes, and related resources.

Used for:

StorageClass: Define storage backend.

PersistentVolumeClaim: Request storage from a specific class.

Example
apiVersion: storage.k8s.io/v1
kind: StorageClass
metadata:
  name: fast-storage
provisioner: kubernetes.io/aws-ebs

5️⃣ Configuration & Autoscaling
apiVersion: autoscaling/v2

Used for scaling applications automatically.

Used for:

HorizontalPodAutoscaler: Scales pods based on CPU/memory usage.

Example
apiVersion: autoscaling/v2
kind: HorizontalPodAutoscaler
metadata:
  name: nginx-hpa
spec:
  scaleTargetRef:
    apiVersion: apps/v1
    kind: Deployment
    name: nginx
  minReplicas: 2
  maxReplicas: 10

6️⃣ Security & Access Control
6.1 RBAC
apiVersion: rbac.authorization.k8s.io/v1

Used to define roles and permissions.

Used for:

Role: Permissions within a namespace.

ClusterRole: Cluster-wide permissions.

Example
apiVersion: rbac.authorization.k8s.io/v1
kind: Role
metadata:
  name: pod-reader
rules:
  - apiGroups: [""]
    resources: ["pods"]
    verbs: ["get", "list"]

6.2 Pod Security
apiVersion: policy/v1

For defining pod disruption budgets and security policies.

7️⃣ Batch Jobs & CronJobs
apiVersion: batch/v1

Used for managing batch and scheduled jobs.

Used for:

Job: One-time tasks.

CronJob: Scheduled tasks.

Example
apiVersion: batch/v1
kind: CronJob
metadata:
  name: backup-job
spec:
  schedule: "0 2 * * *"

8️⃣ Custom Resources (CRDs)
apiVersion: <group>/<version>

Used by operators and for creating custom Kubernetes resources.

9️⃣ Quick Cheat Sheet
Category	apiVersion
Core Objects	v1
Applications	apps/v1
Networking	networking.k8s.io/v1
Storage	storage.k8s.io/v1
Autoscaling	autoscaling/v2
Jobs	batch/v1
Security (RBAC)	rbac.authorization.k8s.io/v1
Custom Resources	<custom-group>/v1
